        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Taiping Rebellion</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">Southern and central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guangxi">Guangxi</a>, where it began at Jintian; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hunan">Hunan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hubei">Hubei</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jiangxi">Jiangxi</a> and Anhui along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangtze-river">Yangtze</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanjing">Nanjing</a>, its capital as Tianjing; southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jiangsu">Jiangsu</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhejiang">Zhejiang</a>, the wealthiest region of the empire; with remnants in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fujian">Fujian</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guangdong">Guangdong</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sichuan">Sichuan</a> and on the Sino-Vietnamese border.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">The God Worshipping Society from 1844; the Jintian uprising, 1850–1851; the march north and down the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangtze-river">Yangtze</a>, 1851–1853; the Heavenly Kingdom at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanjing">Nanjing</a>, 1853–1864, with the failed Northern Expedition and the Tianjing Incident of 1856; the siege and fall of Nanjing, 1862–1864; the last Taiping forces, defeated in 1866 and 1871.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Leading figures</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hong-xiuquan">Hong Xiuquan</a>, the Heavenly King; Feng Yunshan, founder of the God Worshipping Society; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yang-xiuqing">Yang Xiuqing</a>, who claimed to speak as God the Father; Xiao Chaogui; Wei Changhui; Shi Dakai; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hong-rengan">Hong Rengan</a>, Hong’s cousin; Li Xiucheng, the Loyal King; against them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeng-guofan">Zeng Guofan</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiang-army">Xiang Army</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zuo-zongtang">Zuo Zongtang</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/li-hongzhang">Li Hongzhang</a>.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Heavenly Kingdom destroyed with the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanjing">Nanjing</a> in July 1864, in a war whose dead are most widely estimated at 20 to 30 million; a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing dynasty</a> weakened in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and forced to rely on Han <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gentry">gentry</a> and their provincial armies; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/self-strengthening-movement">Self-Strengthening Movement</a>.</span></div>
