    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hong-xiuquan">Hong Xiuquan</a>, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hakka-people">Hakka</a> who had failed the imperial examinations, came to believe from visions and Christian pamphlets that he was the younger brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesus">Jesus Christ</a>, sent to rid the world of demons, among them the Qing.</li><li>From <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanjing">Nanjing</a>, renamed Tianjing, the Taiping Heavenly Kingdom ruled nearly 30 million people at its peak and announced radical reforms: strict separation of the sexes, the abolition of foot binding, land socialisation and a ban on opium.</li><li>Fought as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/total-war">total war</a> with extreme brutality on both sides, it was the deadliest civil war in history: the most widely cited estimates give 20 to 30 million dead, others as many as 100 million.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hong-xiuquan">Hong Xiuquan</a> had studied the Bible in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guangzhou">Guangzhou</a> with the American Baptist missionary Issachar Jacox Roberts, who refused to baptise him; in 1861 Roberts came to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanjing">Nanjing</a>, and Hong made him his director of foreign affairs.</p></aside>
    </section>

